### Optional native decompiler

`third_party/ghidra/` contains a pinned subset of Ghidra developed by the
US National Security Agency and Ghidra contributors, under Apache-2.0.
Original source and parser-generator notices are retained. See
`third_party/ghidra/LICENSE`, `third_party/ghidra/README.md`, and `PINNED.md`.

`binfera-ghidra/data/winapi64.pack` is a compact transformation of function and
type definitions in Ghidra's bundled data type archives (`windows_vs12_64.gdt`
and `generic_clib_64.gdt`, Ghidra 12.1.4, Apache-2.0). Those archives were
produced by the Ghidra project from Windows SDK and C library headers.
Regeneration steps are in `scripts/decompiler_types/README.md`.

The Windows prototype packs also contain a transformation of public-domain DDK
headers from MinGW-w64 14.0.0 (including ReactOS contributors' headers) and
ReactOS 0.4.15-release sdk/include/ddk/fltkernel.h, contributed by Amine Khaldi.
These headers are offered without warranty. Source links, pinned input and
regeneration instructions are in scripts/decompiler_types/README.md.

### Components bundled with the web and desktop apps

The browser and desktop apps (not the command-line tool) ship the following
third-party components in addition to the material above.

**7-Zip.** Archive reading uses 7-Zip, Copyright (C) Igor Pavlov, through the
`7z-wasm` package (https://github.com/use-strict/7z-wasm), which builds the
7-Zip sources (https://www.7-zip.org/) to WebAssembly without modification.
7-Zip is licensed under the GNU LGPL version 2.1 or later, with the unRAR
restriction: the RAR decompression code is derived from unRAR, Copyright (C)
Alexander Roshal, and **may not be used to develop a RAR (WinRAR) compatible
archiver**. The exact version is pinned in `web/package-lock.json`, and the
full licence texts ship in that package as `License.txt` and
`unRarLicense.txt`. The module is a separate file loaded at run time and can be
replaced by rebuilding the app from this repository.

**zip.js** (https://github.com/gildas-lormeau/zip.js), BSD 3-Clause, and
**React** (https://react.dev), MIT.

**Desktop app only.** Tauri (https://tauri.app), Apache-2.0 or MIT. Content
type detection uses Magika (https://github.com/google/magika), Copyright Google
LLC, Apache-2.0, including its model, run with ONNX Runtime
(https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime), Copyright Microsoft Corporation,
MIT, through the `ort` crate. The desktop app also links unmodified crates
under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (`cssparser`, `cssparser-macros`,
`selectors`, `dtoa-short`, `option-ext`); their source is available from
crates.io at the versions pinned in `web/src-tauri/Cargo.lock`.

Every other dependency is under a permissive licence (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD,
Zlib or equivalent); `Cargo.lock`, `web/src-tauri/Cargo.lock` and
`web/package-lock.json` list them with exact versions.
